const data = {
  metaTitle: "Xero & MYOB Integration Developers Australia | AWLabs",
  metaDescription: "Custom Xero and MYOB integrations for Australian businesses: connect your CRM, job system, store or platform with GST, tracking and reconciliation done right.",
  category: "Integration",
  serviceName: "Xero and MYOB Integration",
  nounPhrase: "Xero and MYOB integration",
  involveHeading: "What does a custom Xero or MYOB integration involve?",
  whyHeading: "Why have engineers build your accounting integration?",
  techHeading: "Which APIs and tools do we build Xero and MYOB integrations with?",
  processHeading: "How do we deliver an accounting integration?",
  whoHeading: "Which businesses need a custom Xero or MYOB integration?",
  fitHeading: "Do you need a custom integration, or will an app do?",
  faqHeading: "Common questions about Xero and MYOB integrations",
  slug: "xero-myob-integration",
  heroHeadline: "Xero and MYOB Integrations That Your Bookkeeper Can Actually Reconcile",
  heroTagline: "We build custom integrations between Xero or MYOB and the rest of your business: CRMs, job management, ecommerce, payroll, inventory and your own platforms. Invoices, payments and contacts flow automatically, with GST, tracking categories and failures handled properly.",
  summaryStatement: "A custom Xero or MYOB integration is software that connects an accounting file to another system through the vendor's API, so that invoices, bills, payments, contacts and items move between them automatically, with the accounting rules, error handling and audit trail that a bookkeeper and an auditor need.",
  description: [
    "Most businesses reach for an app first, and they should. The Xero App Store and the MYOB App Marketplace list a wide range of ready made connectors, and for a common pairing, such as a popular ecommerce platform or payroll product, an existing app is usually the cheapest and quickest answer. A custom integration earns its place when the app does not exist, when it does not support the way you work, or when it gets the accounting wrong: the wrong GST code on mixed supplies, sales landing in one lump account instead of by tracking category, duplicate contacts, or a sync that silently stops and is only noticed at BAS time.",
    "The commonest requests we see are connecting Xero or MYOB to a CRM so a won deal becomes an invoice; to job management software such as ServiceM8 or simPRO where the standard sync does not fit; to a custom portal or SaaS product so customers are invoiced automatically; to inventory and purchasing systems; and to several entities at once for consolidated reporting. The design question that matters most is direction. A one way push, where your system creates invoices in Xero, is far simpler and safer than a two way sync where both systems can change the same record, because a two way sync needs rules for which side wins, how deletions and voids are handled, and how to stop records bouncing back and forth.",
    "Each platform sets limits that shape the design. At the time of writing (November 2026), Xero's developer pricing page lists a Starter plan of up to 5 connections at no charge with an API limit of 1,000 calls per day per organisation, and paid plans from $35 AUD a month (Core, up to 50 connections) to $1,445 AUD a month (Advanced, up to 10,000 connections), each with 5,000 calls per day per organisation and a monthly data allowance, with higher tiers requiring app certification and a security assessment. A private integration for one business usually fits comfortably in the Starter limits if it is designed to batch and cache; a product that many businesses will connect needs the plan and certification costs in its business case. MYOB's Business API serves both MYOB Business and AccountRight files, with separate APIs for MYOB Acumatica and EXO, and an AccountRight file stored locally is reached differently from one in the cloud.",
    "The accounting has to be right, not just the data transfer. That means mapping each product or service to the correct account, tax rate and tracking category; handling GST for businesses registered for it (the ATO requires registration once GST turnover reaches $75,000, or $150,000 for non profits); rounding the way the accounting file expects; and dealing with multiple currencies and entities where they apply. We agree the mapping with your accountant or bookkeeper before we write code, and every sync writes a log they can read. Senior engineers lead every build and review every change, and you receive updates every Tuesday and Friday, Sydney time.",
  ],
  benefits: [
    {
      icon: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 1l4 4-4 4"/><path d="M3 11V9a4 4 0 0 1 4-4h14"/><path d="M7 23l-4-4 4-4"/><path d="M21 13v2a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H3"/></svg>',
      title: 'Right Direction, Right Rules',
      description: 'We decide with you which system owns each record. One way pushes where possible, two way sync only where it is genuinely needed, with explicit rules for conflicts, voids, credit notes and deletions, so nothing is overwritten by surprise.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="2" width="16" height="20" rx="2"/><line x1="8" y1="6" x2="16" y2="6"/><line x1="8" y1="10" x2="10" y2="10"/><line x1="14" y1="10" x2="16" y2="10"/><line x1="8" y1="14" x2="10" y2="14"/><line x1="14" y1="14" x2="16" y2="14"/><line x1="8" y1="18" x2="16" y2="18"/></svg>',
      title: 'Accounting Your Bookkeeper Signs Off',
      description: 'Accounts, tax rates, tracking categories, items and rounding are mapped with your accountant before build. Invoices land coded the way they would be entered by hand, so reconciliation and BAS preparation get easier, not harder.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>',
      title: 'Failures That Get Noticed',
      description: 'Expired connections, rejected invoices, locked periods and API limits are caught, retried where safe and reported to a named person straight away. A sync that stops quietly for three weeks is the most expensive kind of integration bug.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>',
      title: 'Reconciliation Reports',
      description: 'A daily or weekly report compares totals in both systems and lists anything that did not match, with a link to the record. Your bookkeeper sees the gap before month end instead of hunting for it.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/></svg>',
      title: 'Designed Around API Limits',
      description: 'Batching, caching, webhooks and queueing keep the integration well inside Xero and MYOB limits, including during busy periods and the first bulk import, so a sales spike does not stall your invoicing.',
    },
    {
      icon: '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>',
      title: 'Secure Access to Financial Data',
      description: 'OAuth connections with the narrowest scopes the job needs, tokens stored encrypted, no shared logins, and a clear record of who connected which file. Financial data is hosted in Australian cloud regions where your Schedule of Work requires it.',
    },
  ],
