  faqs: [
    {
      question: 'Is there already an app that connects my system to Xero or MYOB?',
      answer: 'Check first; often there is. Search the Xero App Store or the MYOB App Marketplace for your other system, and ask that vendor whether they have a native integration. If an app exists and codes transactions the way your accountant wants, use it. We recommend a custom build when no app exists, when the app cannot handle your accounts, tracking or multiple entities, or when you need the integration inside your own product.',
    },
    {
      question: 'What does Xero charge developers to use its API?',
      answer: 'At the time of writing (November 2026), Xero\'s developer pricing page lists five plans. Starter is at no charge for up to 5 connections with 1,000 API calls per day per organisation. Core is $35 AUD a month for up to 50 connections, Plus $245 AUD for up to 1,000, Advanced $1,445 AUD for up to 10,000, and Enterprise is priced on application. Paid plans allow 5,000 calls per day per organisation and include a monthly data egress allowance, with overage at $2.40 AUD per GB. Prices are tax exclusive and change, so check developer.xero.com before you budget.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Can you integrate with MYOB AccountRight on a desktop?',
      answer: 'Yes, with some extra work. MYOB\'s Business API serves both cloud files and AccountRight files, but a file stored locally is reached through a local API on the network where it lives, not through MYOB\'s cloud endpoint. In practice most businesses we would advise are moving to cloud files, which makes the integration simpler and more reliable. MYOB Acumatica and MYOB EXO have their own APIs.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Should the integration sync both ways?',
      answer: 'Only where it must. A one way flow, for example invoices created in your job system and pushed to Xero, with payment status read back, covers most needs and is much easier to keep correct. A full two way sync of the same records needs rules for which side wins every conflict, and is where most integration problems come from. We will tell you plainly when one way is enough.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How do you make sure GST is right?',
      answer: 'We map every product, service and fee to the tax rate your accountant specifies, test mixed supplies, GST free items, discounts and rounding against a demo file, and compare totals before go live. Under ATO rules a business must register for GST once its GST turnover reaches $75,000, or $150,000 for a non profit, and the integration follows your registration status. Your accountant remains responsible for the tax treatment; we make sure the software applies it consistently.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Can you connect several Xero organisations or entities?',
      answer: 'Yes. Each organisation is a separate connection with its own API limits, accounts and tax settings, so the integration routes each transaction to the right entity and keeps the mappings separate. For groups we can also build consolidated reporting that reads from every entity in one place.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Are you a Xero or MYOB partner?',
      answer: 'We do not hold a Xero or MYOB partner status, and we do not need one to build a private integration for your business. We build against the vendors\' published APIs under their developer terms. If you are building a product to list on the Xero App Store, Xero\'s certification and plan requirements apply to your app, and we build to them with you.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How much does a custom Xero integration cost?',
      answer: 'It depends on the number of record types, the direction of sync, the systems on the other side and the volume of transactions. Every build starts with a Discovery Audit, a fixed fee credited in full against the build. After two strategy sessions you receive a fixed price Schedule of Work with three options: The Minimum, The Recommended and The Complete. Our workflow automation cost guide covers typical Australian market ranges for integration work; those are market figures, not our prices.',
    },
    {
      question: "Can you connect ServiceM8 or simPRO to Xero?",
      answer: "Yes, when the standard sync doesn't fit how you work. ServiceM8 and simPRO both offer their own Xero connections, so check those first. We build custom integrations when you need invoices split by tracking category, jobs linked to the right entity, materials coded to specific accounts, or data the standard connector doesn't carry, using each platform's published API. We agree the account and tax mapping with your bookkeeper before building.",
    },
    {
      question: "Should our integration be built for Xero or MYOB?",
      answer: "Build for the accounting system your business and your accountant already use, because switching systems for an integration is rarely worth it. Both offer published APIs that support custom integrations, with different limits and file types: Xero is cloud only, while MYOB serves cloud files and AccountRight files that may sit on a local network. If you sell software to many businesses, supporting both widens your market, and we design the integration layer so a second platform can be added.",
    },
    {
      question: "Do we need a custom integration for bank feeds into Xero?",
      answer: "Usually not. Xero connects bank feeds for many Australian banks directly, so check Xero's own bank feeds list before commissioning anything. Custom work comes in around the feed, for example matching payments from a gateway or your own system to invoices so reconciliation is quick, or posting payout fees and refunds to the right accounts. We look at your reconciliation process before recommending code.",
    },
  ],
  comparison: {
    rightFor: [
      'No app connects your system to Xero or MYOB, or the app codes transactions wrongly',
      'Staff retype invoices, bills or payments between systems every week',
      'You need tracking categories, several entities or multiple currencies handled automatically',
      'Your own software product needs to invoice customers through their own or your Xero file',
      'You want reconciliation reports and alerts instead of finding sync problems at BAS time',
    ],
    notRightFor: [
      'A well reviewed app already does exactly what you need at a modest monthly fee',
      'You have a few dozen transactions a month, where manual entry costs less than any build',
      'Your chart of accounts and coding rules are still in flux; settle those with your accountant first',
      'You are about to change accounting platform, in which case integrate after the move',
      'You want the integration to make tax decisions, which belong with your accountant',
    ],
  },
  definitions: [
    {
      term: 'Accounting Integration',
      definition: 'Software that moves transactions and records between an accounting file, such as Xero or MYOB, and another system through the vendor\'s API, applying the agreed accounting rules.',
    },
    {
      term: 'One Way Push',
      definition: 'An integration where one system creates or updates records in the other, but not the reverse. Simpler and safer than a two way sync.',
    },
    {
      term: 'Two Way Sync',
      definition: 'An integration where both systems can change the same records and keep each other up to date. It needs explicit rules for conflicts and deletions.',
    },
    {
      term: 'Tracking Category',
      definition: 'A Xero feature for tagging transactions by department, location, job or other dimension, so reports can be split without extra accounts.',
    },
    {
      term: 'Reconciliation Report',
      definition: 'A scheduled comparison of totals and records between the two systems that lists anything that does not match, so errors are found early.',
    },
  ],
  sources: [
    { title: 'Xero Developer pricing and policies', url: 'https://developer.xero.com/pricing', publisher: 'Xero' },
    { title: 'MYOB Business API: getting started', url: 'https://developer.myob.com/api/myob-business-api/api-overview/getting-started/', publisher: 'MYOB' },
